      "seconds": 89.18,
      "answer": "**The Water Cycle: A Journey for Water**\n\nDo you know what happens to the water in the lake when the sun shines? Let's follow the water's journey through the water cycle!\n\n**Evaporation: Water Turns into Air**\nImagine you're taking a hot shower. The water on your skin turns into air, right? That's kind of like what happens when the sun warms the water in lakes. Some of the water turns into water vapor and rises into the air.\n\n**Condensation: Air Becomes Water**\nNow, imagine you breathe onto a cold window. The air on your breath turns into tiny drops of water, right? That's what happens when the air with water vapor cools down and turns back into liquid water. This creates clouds!\n\n**Precipitation: Water Falls Back to Earth**\nImagine you're playing with a big bucket of water. When the bucket gets too full, the water starts to spill over, right? That's kind of like what happens when the water in the clouds gets too heavy. It falls back to Earth as rain!\n\nAnd then... the water returns to the lake, and the cycle starts all over again!\n\n> Coverage check: 3 of 3 source sections have no linked substantive passage in this answer. The response may be incomplete; full coverage is not verified.",
